{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:06:48.231266Z","id":"b041ea0214dec031a8df84775b2ec9e7cea7beb5e8eef5ad12882ffaba34a5b2","body":{"detail":"PromptBuilder.change writes CommentContext.anchorLine verbatim after \"Anchored on: \", while the comment body and author are JSON-quoted. The anchor's quote is page text (which the agent itself wrote, or which a document rendered), so it can carry instruction-like text or newlines that break the prompt's layout. Whoever renders anchorLine (the feedback worker in lib/agent/loop.dart) should JSON-quote the quote part and cut it to 120 characters, or PromptBuilder should quote the whole line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"72d1d0918b41b8390e360792f83ec31640d348c6f9cf350c9e988e603fd4dee8"},"summary":"The anchor line goes into the change prompt unquoted, though its quote is text taken from the page","tags":["security","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:06:48.231479Z","id":"1d76d70ec363a2b25c56d46a32ab274f275e2b1a62ef7c55878a3680785520bb","body":{"detail":"Two FileWrite entries with the same path, or a path in both files and removed, pass validation (the rules in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md Task F4a do not list them). The code that applies a result (applyResult) must give these a defined meaning (last write wins; removed after files, or a refusal) and test it, or validateResult should refuse them with a named reason so the one retry can fix them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"3199a4dbb21944535df116037febfe986383332e2f390bd23376fd97c4286edc"},"summary":"validateResult does not refuse a path written twice in files, or both written and removed","tags":["validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968137Z","id":"02408d6b80a7ca649671c41c4a511cca863557e94ffc752a5601f0aa5941d775","body":{"detail":"Failure: a result with db [{op: 'set', collection: 'runs', doc_id: 'my run', data_json: '{}'}] (or doc_id '..', 'é', a 201-byte segment, or a collection deeper than 16 segments) passes validateResult. The daemon's segment rule (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs:88-96, segment_ok: ASCII letters, digits and _ - . ~ : @ +, 1 to 200 bytes, not . or ..; db.rs:98-117: at most 1000 bytes and 16 segments per path) refuses it with invalid_argument. Spec section 3.6 applies a change as publish, then the db operations, so the new version is already live when docs:batch fails: a shape migration the new page depends on never runs, and a daemon 400 is not a validation failure, so the one retry with the failure named does not happen. validateResult should apply the same segment and length rules to collection + '/' + doc_id, naming the bad segment, with a test case per rule in test/agent/edit_result_test.dart.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"129583594e693adaa0ba0265c5fc87b263e7865675e1d38445b7ad5c9050ed0a"},"summary":"validateResult accepts db collection and doc_id segments that the daemon refuses, so a change publishes and then its db writes fail","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968319Z","id":"5f0eadcd4a81e91d233c2802156851d44716a1dd32c303f11ab8589d44296b9a","body":{"detail":"_checkPath refuses code units below 0x20 and 0x7f only. crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:96-117 (check_path) also refuses every char::is_control character (U+0080 to U+009F) and U+2028/U+2029. Such a path passes validation and the publish or create then fails with invalid_path, which is not retried with the reason named. Mirror the daemon's rule (and add test cases for '\\u0085' and '\\u2028').","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"629ba97c204ed9557d56e9218c01cc470ae9101a14151ad960ff01f5aef74111"},"summary":"File paths with C1 control characters or U+2028/U+2029 pass validateResult but the daemon refuses them","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_schema.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968419Z","id":"0f5e9d556f451b80d34ae63ddb6a29c1833e998e32330255becffb5eff044536","body":{"detail":"claude 2.1.296 implements --json-schema as a synthetic StructuredOutput tool that the model must call (strings in the binary: 'StructuredOutput enforcement failed', 'structuredOutputTool'), passed separately from the tools option, so it probably survives --tools \"\", but nothing in `claude --help` says so and no test exercises it. The schema itself is plain JSON Schema with a top-level object, which that path accepts. The ClaudeCliBackend's integration run must confirm that a `--tools \"\" --json-schema <editSchema>` call returns `structured_output`, and fall back to parsing `result` if it does not (spec section 3.6).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"7c4f21fb9cdc049af71174832ed6c1e28607669a87b512e96c980dc7ab0402fa"},"summary":"The schema's use as claude -p --json-schema together with --tools \"\" is unverified","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968595Z","id":"9d7b7a03bde2489160cd1a2aa01a668a6186e65f7454ec3bf79e902eb074e800","body":{"detail":"AgentRequest.image carries the first comment's PNG clip and the Messages API backend sends it as an image block before the text (spec section 3.6), but the text never mentions it, so the model has to guess what the picture is. One line under the first comment when a clip is present ('The image shows the region this comment is anchored on.') ties them together; the claude -p backend sends no image, so the line belongs only when the request carries one.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"861b735f905659c696c9ca336459debd260b8b34e878cc799c78e21dd11d952c"},"summary":"The change prompt does not say that an attached image is the first comment's clip","tags":["review","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968682Z","id":"e5dc33c948f91302fb4934ba397906d5c58529f1df3551eeab125afb276af332","body":{"detail":"Spec section 8 says comment text and documents go in the prompt as JSON strings. The anchor's quote is page text, which can include the person's documents or other apps' data rendered on the page, and a newline in it can forge a 'Comment:' line or a new section. Quoting the whole line where it is written (prompt.dart:119, jsonEncode(c.anchorLine)) keeps the property in one place with its test; leaving it to lib/agent/loop.dart spreads it across two files. test/agent/prompt_test.dart:176 pins the unquoted form and changes with it; add a case with a newline and 'Comment:' in the anchor.","kind":"comment","references":"b041ea0214dec031a8df84775b2ec9e7cea7beb5e8eef5ad12882ffaba34a5b2","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"72d1d0918b41b8390e360792f83ec31640d348c6f9cf350c9e988e603fd4dee8"},"summary":"Review: fix this in PromptBuilder now, not in the feedback worker","tags":["review","security","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968758Z","id":"13b1ee98d89d02c5beac97e8eb62d457ca1a77beaa463a04fe5e03cfd08abf53","body":{"detail":"validateResult is the gate before anything is published, and the code that applies a result does not exist yet. Refusing (1) the same path twice in files, (2) a path both in files and in removed, and (3) an edit on a path in removed, each with a named reason, lets the one retry fix them and leaves the applier a single meaning to implement. Two edits on the same path stay allowed: they apply in order.","kind":"comment","references":"1d76d70ec363a2b25c56d46a32ab274f275e2b1a62ef7c55878a3680785520bb","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"3199a4dbb21944535df116037febfe986383332e2f390bd23376fd97c4286edc"},"summary":"Review: refuse these in validateResult now","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549213Z","id":"c722498e8c28082955b686e9e128bd55735af2e14e12ba62f519521ba8367b34","body":{"detail":"MessagesApiBackend.run sends one request and throws AgentError(retryable: true) on 408/429/5xx (line 143), on a timeout and on an IOException. Nothing in lib/agent reads AgentError.retryable: the change flow in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md (Task F4b, 'backend error replies with the reason and acks') turns any backend error into a 'Couldn't make that change' reply. A brief 529 overload on the phone therefore fails the person's change outright, where the official SDKs retry twice with backoff.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"4790ee6a638e70b8996da7eeed0be8340a3929e8ea7f8a9efc28b2bb9444f1e8"},"suggested_fix":"Retry once or twice on retryable errors with backoff, honouring the retry-after header, either here (with an injected delay so tests stay deterministic) or in AgentLoop before replying.","summary":"A retryable Messages API failure (429, 529, 5xx, timeout, unreachable) is never retried","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549410Z","id":"2ab7d46469be3dfc22538fa516e427a2d6d35342a609edd1db5f4b3237a5f93e","body":{"detail":"A new app's whole index.html travels inside one JSON string; at about 3-4 characters per token, 16000 output tokens (thinking included) is roughly 50 KB of result. A larger app stops with stop_reason max_tokens, which run() reports as the non-retryable 'The result was too long' (line 170). maxResultBytes in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart is 8 MiB, so the two limits disagree by two orders of magnitude. Raising max_tokens past about 16000 needs streaming to stay under HTTP timeouts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"7ee51ed7d3fafff2c82f26e2446099a8fdb900be72907249ae3a01a29c6a2a22"},"suggested_fix":"Stream the response (SSE) and raise max_tokens (Haiku 5.5 allows 128K), or tell the model the output budget in system.md so it prefers edits and compact apps.","summary":"max_tokens 16000 caps a result far below what validateResult allows (8 MiB)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549536Z","id":"434383b69743e08280d24834604909326725b112a2a6bdc0e3790b9a27282c8a","body":{"detail":"The request body is exactly the one docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md gives for Task F5, with no anthropic-beta header and no fallbacks parameter. The default model claude-haiku-5-5 has no server-side fallback, so a refusal is final and run() throws a non-retryable AgentError naming its category. claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-opus-5-5, offered in settings, accept fallbacks: \"default\" with the server-side-fallback-2026-07-01 beta header, which would re-run a declined request on another model inside the same call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"a75c696ef485d8913e7d7a6104527cbdbfa2c80f8fb272077040142b73ca0f4f"},"summary":"Server-side refusal fallbacks (the fallbacks request parameter) are not sent","tags":["revisit:refusals are seen in practice with claude-sonnet-5-5 or claude-opus-5-5 selected","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
